From: Wine Fox
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Zero attributes in FileBasicInformation leave them as they are.

SetFileTime() passes FileBasicInformation with FileAttributes 0, which on Windows means "do
not change the attributes". Wine treated it as "clear FILE_ATTRIBUTE_READONLY" and made
read-only files writable when their times were set (Perforce's noallwrite workspaces).

Wine 11.22 lets the owner open a read-only file for FILE_WRITE_ATTRIBUTES on its own (server:
"Don't require Unix write access to change file attributes", Wine-Bug 56925), so the server
half of the 11.7 patch is gone.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
index d99a9a1..b64329f 100755
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
@@ -4912,7 +4912,9 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtSetInformationFile( HANDLE handle, IO_STATUS_BLOCK *io,
             if (atime.QuadPart || mtime.QuadPart)
                 status = set_file_times( fd, &mtime, &atime );
 
-            if (status == STATUS_SUCCESS)
+            /* zero attributes leave them as they are (SetFileTime passes zero): not a request
+             * to clear FILE_ATTRIBUTE_READONLY */
+            if (status == STATUS_SUCCESS && info->FileAttributes)
                 status = fd_set_file_info( fd, info->FileAttributes,
                                            unix_name && is_hidden_file( unix_name ));
 
